.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
*.egg

# ----- Trade Journal (local measurement DB, not source) -----
trade_journal.db
telemetry.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# NOTE: there is deliberately no blanket `*.db` rule here — only named files. So a
# NEW SQLite store added to a service is NOT ignored by default and will show up in
# `git status` ready to be committed by accident. Add it below when you add one.
# (CLAUDE.md section 11 claims a `*.db` rule exists. It does not.)

# ----- Find Quant Trade session store + LangGraph checkpoints -----
# Both hold USER DATA and neither belongs in git: sessions.db is the conversation
# record (user ids, questions, transcripts, trade plans) and checkpoints.db is the
# agent's model context and tool state for those conversations. In production they
# live on the deep_quant_data volume at /data; these entries catch the local-default
# paths beside the module, which is where a test run or a `python main.py` puts them.
# The -wal / -shm sidecars exist because both are opened in WAL mode.
sessions.db
sessions.db-wal
sessions.db-shm
checkpoints.db
checkpoints.db-wal
checkpoints.db-shm

# ----- Compliance record (P2 recommendation record + P5 interaction log) -----
# NEVER commit this. It is the append-only regulatory record: it holds user ids
# and published recommendations, it is subject to a 5-year SEBI retention floor,
# and a copy in git history could not be corrected or erased. It belongs in the
# off-machine backup the rotation runbook describes, not in the repository.
# The -wal / -shm sidecars exist because hashchain.py opens the store in WAL mode.
compliance.db
compliance.db-wal
compliance.db-shm

# ----- Runtime caches written by services -----
# The aggregator persists its Kite instrument dump next to the binary so the
# cache survives a restart (kite_api.rs::disk_cache_path). It is ~12 MB of
# regenerable exchange data, refetched automatically once the 24h TTL lapses,
# so committing it would add bulk to every clone to no purpose — and would go
# stale immediately, since contract listings change daily.
aggregator/instruments_cache_*.json

